data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","item_id":"rs_0a6f517af0616dc3016ac27161aeb08190b502a13164ab04dd","output_index":0,"sequence_number":193,"summary_index":1,"text":"**Checking number properties**\n\nI’m examining the number 1061 to see if it’s prime. I find that when I add 2 and 6, I get 1063 and 1067, which could also be primes. To confirm if 1061 is prime, I check its divisibility against smaller primes like 2, 3, 5, and 7. It seems likely prime since none of those smaller numbers divide it evenly. It’s fascinating how these calculations work together to find potential primes!"}

